&lt;p&gt;Embracing the complete range of skills and services across the communications spectrum without constraint, we create the best outcomes for our clients and deliver world-class work.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Hanover is actively seeking a highly experienced and dynamic Account Director to become an integral part of our Healthcare Policy, Advocacy &amp;amp; Public Affairs team. This is an exceptional opportunity for someone to leverage their expertise in the healthcare sector and make a significant impact on our client services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Account Director, you will lead client relationships, providing senior strategic counsel and ensuring delivery of high-quality, commercially successful account programmes. You will guide clients through the complex landscape of healthcare policy, advocacy, and public affairs, while leading account teams and overseeing programme delivery and budgets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will play a leading role in new business activity, including acquisition, development and pitching, alongside managing and mentoring junior team members.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role will be based in London and offers the opportunity to work across clients we share with our offices in Brussels, Dublin and the Middle East, as well as integrated accounts with our Healthcare Communications and Digital teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team works across a range of services including government relations, public affairs, market access, policy, advocacy and corporate communications across health and business. With over half of the world’s top 20 pharmaceutical companies, as well as NHS providers, health technology businesses and charities amongst our clients, we offer a diverse and compelling range of issues and opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead client accounts, ensuring high-quality delivery, strong client satisfaction and commercial performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead high-impact political and NHS campaigns to deliver tangible policy change for our clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead high-profile events and stakeholder engagement programmes involving politicians, policymakers, NHS stakeholders and patient groups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver high-quality strategic intelligence and insights to our clients by utilising the Hanover network and building your own network and expertise across policy areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain an uncompromising commitment to detail, rigorously reviewing all communications, reports and client deliverables to ensure accuracy and professionalism.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to grow existing client relationships and broaden Hanover’s offer across accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement innovative strategies for growth, staying ahead of industry trends and positioning Hanover as a leader in the field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take a lead on new business pitches, being a core part of the team in building creative strategies and tactics and pitching to clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver marketing activity to support Hanover Health’s business growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the management of expert steering groups to drive thought-leadership for our clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personal management of junior members of the team providing guidance on professional development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active participant in championing the mission, vision, purpose, values and behaviours of Hanover.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recognise and value the diverse backgrounds, skills, and perspectives of all individuals at Hanover.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant experience from a public affairs consultancy, in-house public affairs department, patient group/NGO, Parliament, or other relevant organisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent knowledge of health policy and ability to analyse developments within the NHS and commercial environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of success in account management within the healthcare policy, advocacy, or public affairs sector.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eye for detail and ability to think critically about your own work and that of others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional leadership skills with the ability to inspire and guide teams towards achieving shared goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen with experience in managing budgets and driving business growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong strategic judgement and ability to provide credible counsel to senior clients in complex and fast-moving policy environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, capable of building rapport with clients, team members, and stakeholders at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A commitment to professional development, both for self-improvement and for the mentorship of junior colleagues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BENEFITS:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to a competitive salary, your core benefits package will include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus potential linked to recruitment, new business and long service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days’ annual leave (plus bank holidays)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private healthcare and dental insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A company pension plan, including 5% employer contribution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll also have access to a wide range of opportunities and initiatives, including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working policies, plus eligibility to apply for a sabbatical after 2 years’ service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Summer Fridays finish (3pm) – early Friday finish the rest of the year (4pm)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Hanover Academy, which incorporates training, coaching, mentoring and reverse-mentoring opportunities to support personal development and career progression across all levels, with a generous training budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;International secondments as well as the opportunity to collaborate with all offices across the AVENIR GLOBAL’s network&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A wellbeing programme, featuring (but not limited to) pre- and post-maternity leave coaching, a working parents’ group, subsidised gym membership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our Culture Club, with a robust social calendar all year round and CSR activity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity, Equity and Inclusion Statement +&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hanover Communications is an equal opportunities employer, committed to creating and ensuring a fair, inclusive, and diverse work environment where all individuals are treated with respect and dignity. We believe that equality and diversity are essential to high performance and a thriving culture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We maintain a strict no-tolerance stance against any form of discrimination and harassment, ensuring all individuals are treated equitably, irrespective of their race, ethnicity, religion, beliefs, age, sex, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, disability, marital or pregnancy status, genetic background, or any other attribute safeguarded under our company policies or federal, state or local laws and legislation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We want to ensure that our hiring process is accessible. If you need reasonable accommodation for any part of the application process, please send an email to &lt;a ---------- with the nature of your request.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are committed to transparency about how we collect and use your data, including ensuring we comply with legal obligations relating to data protection. You can view our data privacy policy&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://hanovercomms.com/recruitment-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hanover is part of AVENIR GLOBAL’s powerhouse of specialist communications consultancies across EMEA and North America. Collectively we rank among the top 15 largest communication firms in the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Find out more about &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hanovercomms.com/about-us/&quot;&gt;Hanover&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hanovercomms.com/careers/&quot;&gt;working for us&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Addepar is a global data and AI platform empowering investment professionals to turn complex financial information into actionable intelligence. Addepar unifies portfolio, market and client data in a total portfolio view and delivers AI-powered insights within investment and client workflows. More than 1,400 firms in nearly 60 countries use Addepar to manage and advise on nearly $9 trillion in assets. Its open platform integrates with nearly 650 software, data and consulting partners to power end-to-end investment operations across firms of all sizes and complexity. Addepar supports clients worldwide with offices in New York City, Salt Lake City, London, Edinburgh, Pune, Dubai, Geneva, Singapore and São Paulo.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;The Role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Alts Data Operations is an Addepar team that focuses on Alternatives Investment Data.&amp;nbsp; The team collects and validates information on private funds, private companies and other non-public investments.&amp;nbsp; This data is used for our research projects on investment decision-making and deliver new research products on topics related to investing (e.g., briefs, working papers, journal articles, models). The R&amp;amp;I mission is to inform wealth managers and institutional investors on new ways to improve their investment performance, by helping them augment their governance, management, operations, and processes. The goal is to apply Addepar’s proprietary and private data (both quantitative and qualitative) to bring new and powerful insights to the world of investors.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are currently seeking an Alternatives Data Operations Analyst to work UK hours, joining our growing presence in Pune. This role will be dedicated to capturing and updating Alternatives data to power new innovations developed using a proprietary research platform. The platform aggregates over $9 Trillion in assets into an analytical data store that can be analyzed for new insights by researchers at Addepar and other prominent research institutions (e.g. London School of Economics, Dept. of Finance). The role is responsible for ensuring the platform has timely and high-quality data available. This will include oversight of the alternatives security master, data quality validations management, and workflow oversight.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Applicants must have, and maintain, the right to work in the United Kingdom from the first day of employment. Please note that visa sponsorship is not available for this role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work collaboratively with our UK team investigating Alternative Investment attributes during the UK working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research investments on Addepar’s global database and classify per asset type, vintage, and strategy.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee and manage operational workflows for Alternative data processing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain effective process controls and accurate metrics to ensure quality standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with members of the Research team to implement and run data quality validations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the security master and security classification processes&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own and Optimise Data Pipelines:&lt;/strong&gt; Independently manage and troubleshoot complex end-to-end data ingestion pipelines, resolving technical blockers (e.g., networking, querying, or database errors) in partnership with engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Integrate AI &amp;amp; Developer Tooling:&lt;/strong&gt; Proactively explore and implement AI-assisted developer tools (such as Claude Code or custom LLM prompts) to optimise repetitive workflows, streamline document parsing, and shorten validation cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Who You Are&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience of financial investment/advisory industry with knowledge of capital markets, middle/back-office operations systems, and preferably with experience dealing with Alternatives (Private/Draw-down) Funds reporting statements and data.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detailed in documenting and exhibits good follow-through techniques&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of effective problem-solving abilities, self-motivation to take on responsibility, and a strong team-player mentality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding communication and interpersonal skills for working with clients, custodial data providers, as well as internal working partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical skills preferred in any or all of the following: Microsoft Excel, Google Suite, Atlassian Jira/Confluence, SQL, Python (Jupyter Notebook, Pandas, PySpark, etc.), Databricks, Bloomberg, Pitchbook, or other common financial services systems and applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on SQL &amp;amp; Data Warehouse Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong proficiency using &lt;strong&gt;SQL&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;Databricks (PySpark)&lt;/strong&gt; to navigate complex data architectures, extract custom audits, and validate high-volume datasets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Familiarity with Modern AI Developer Tools:&lt;/strong&gt; Exposure to or a strong interest in using AI tools (e.g., &lt;strong&gt;Claude Code&lt;/strong&gt;, GitHub Copilot, or automated API integrations) to optimize code and speed up daily data operational workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alternative Asset Document Literacy:&lt;/strong&gt; Exceptional ability to interpret unstructured private market financial data (such as Form D filings, capital account statements, or institutional investment briefs) and translate them into clean, structured database taxonomies.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Values&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Act Like an Owner - &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Think and operate with intention, purpose and care. Own outcomes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build Together - &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Collaborate to unlock the best solutions. Deliver lasting value.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Champion Our Clients - &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Exceed client expectations. Our clients’ success is our success.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Innovation - &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Be bold and unconstrained in problem solving. Transform the industry.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Embrace Learning - &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Engage our community to broaden our perspective. Bring a growth mindset.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;In addition to our core values, Addepar is proud to be an equal opportunity employer. We seek to bring together diverse ideas, experiences, skill sets, perspectives, backgrounds and identities to drive innovative solutions. We commit to promoting a welcoming environment where inclusion and belonging are held as a shared responsibility.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We will ensure that individuals with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodation to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and to receive other benefits and privileges of employment. Please contact us to request accommodation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;PHISHING SCAM WARNING: Addepar is among several companies recently made aware of a phishing scam involving con artists posing as hiring managers recruiting via email, text and social media. The imposters are creating misleading email accounts, conducting remote “interviews,” and making fake job offers in order to collect personal and financial information from unsuspecting individuals. Please be aware that no job offers will be made from Addepar without a formal interview process. Additionally, Addepar will not ask you to purchase equipment or supplies as part of your onboarding process. If you have any questions, please reach out to &lt;a ----------<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

